From f9235ffc9e9e28cc5563c82e1435f15e51f6bb29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:04:52 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/60] TP RoCE: TF_TP_ROCE_CHUNKED_KB gathers strides past the
 slot in slot-sized ops, at most 2 MiB in flight

Default off. allGatherV strides past the slot, up to TF_TP_ROCE_CHUNKED_KB, go RoCE as ceil(n / slot) launches of
the tp_roce kernel: op c moves at most a slot of each shard from c x slot (RoceArgs.chunk), and an op empty on both
ranks rings no doorbell and leaves the epoch. Every RDMA write keeps the 1 MiB cap. The kernel poisons the transport
rather than stage past a slot, and its four failure-record blocks fold into fail_record (same stores and fences).

VerbsWire.post waits for completions while the bytes posted and not completed over both HCAs would pass
max_inflight (2 MiB, a constant in the post path); a wait that sees no completion for 10 s fails the proxy. Boot
refuses TF_TP_ROCE_CHUNKED_KB when the kernel image lacks the tp_roce_chunk_abi marker. The setting is part of the
digest both ranks agree on.

Tests: chunked strides from 300 KB to a 128 MiB union posted back to back on fake verbs whose completions lag keep at
most 2 MiB in flight and no write past 1 MiB, and reach the cap; the wire's own in-flight count and peak match the
fake HCAs'. Over the shm wire, 2,000 chunked variable-length gathers of up to four slots arrive bit for bit.

(cherry picked from commit 664a8e2d57549ab9d040a2c4f9e8ce53e274760c)
